 70	const USAGE = `tally: a CFO for a fleet of coding agents
 71	
 72	Usage: tally <command> [options]
 73	
 74	Commands:
 75	  experiment Run baseline and Tally repeats with a shared safety budget
 76	  run      Run the backlog against the budget in tally.yaml
 77	  demo     Run the full loop with simulated workers on a sample backlog
 78	  dashboard Start the local dashboard server
 79	  init     Set up tally.yaml for the current repository
 80	  uninstall List and remove the recorded Tally installation
 81	  doctor   Check that each integration is connected
 82	  login    Connect an integration, e.g. tally login cfoai
 83	  market   Search CrustData for companies adopting coding agents
 84	  publish  Write a static dashboard bundle (does not deploy)
 85	  traces drain --run <id> Drain and read-back verify a finished run's worker traces
 86	
 87	Options:
 88	  --repeats <N>     Repeats per experiment mode (default: 2)
 89	  --config <path>   Path to tally.yaml (default: tally.yaml)
 90	  --dry-run         Simulate workers; spends nothing
 91	  --budget <usd>    Override the budget for this run
 92	  --only <task>     Run a single task
 93	  --baseline        Send every task to the strongest tier
 94	  --dashboard       Start the dashboard server after run/demo
 95	  --open            Alias for --dashboard
 96	  --port <number>   Dashboard port (default: 5177; use 0 for any free port)
 97	  --plan            Size and route tasks, but do not spawn workers
 98	  --live            For demo: use live read-only integrations with fake workers
 99	  --yes             For init: approve the final change summary without prompting
100	  --output <dir>    Output directory for tally market (default: .tally/market/latest)
101	  --limit <number>  Result limit for tally market (default: 10)
102	  --keyword <text>  CrustData keyword for tally market (default: AI coding)
103	  --out <dir>       New directory for tally publish (required)
104	  --runs <ids>      Comma-separated run folder ids (default: all real runs)
105	  --run <id>        Run id for traces drain; --output overrides its run directory
106	  -h, --help        Show this help
107	  -v, --version     Show the version`;
